hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27994","Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Yazid ibn Jabir al-Ansari, from a grandmother of his, she said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered upon her, with a waterskin with her, and drank from its mouth while standing."
"27995","And this hadith was read to him, meaning Sufyan: I heard Yazid, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Amrah, from my grandmother, she being Kubayshah."
